fact WorkItem(id: "WI-825", description: some(value: "FIX the σ-gate's COMPOUND-element blindness (WI-821 /code-review finding 1, CONFIRMED by live drive): the cover pair verdict is HEAD-only — is_type_param_value tests only the head, so a compound element (Wrap[A = CT]) classifies concrete and two same-head compounds with different interiors compare via dispatch_values_match, whose fallback compares head sort symbols with args ignored (types_lesseq REJECTS the pair first, so the head fallback is the ACCEPTING leg; both legs never consult ctx.subst). MEASURED: caller requires Desc[T = Wrap[A = CT]] handing off to a callee dep σ-instantiated to Desc[T = Wrap[A = Wrap[A = CT]]] FORWARDS the shallower dict — single hand-off 12 where 122 is correct; compound-element recursion 12 at EVERY depth (correct 12/122/1222) — the exact pre-WI-821 (d) signature one constructor level deeper. Positive control (no cover in scope) constructs the depth-2 dict correctly (122), so Strategy 3 handles the shape; only the gate lets the forward through. FIX LOCUS is ONE place now: binding_pair_covers (kb/typing.rs — the folded per-pair verdict, whose doc carries a KNOWN LIMIT note pointing here). Rule: under σ, a (c,c) pair whose sides are COMPOUND must compare σ-STRUCTURALLY — same head AND each param-position pair recursively binding_pair_covers-σ (σ-classes at param leaves, dispatch_values_match at ground leaves); head-only acceptance is what re-admits the defect. WATCH: the coarse (None) mode must keep today's head tolerance (diagnostic path); concrete GROUND same-head pairs (Wrap[Int64] vs Wrap[Int64]) must still cover (types_lesseq already accepts identical grounds — verify before relying on the fallback deletion). ACCEPTANCE: the driven fixture (write it as a wi821 test: DeepHolder requires Desc[T = Wrap[A = DT]] hand-off shape from the /code-review verifier) measures 122 and 12/122/1222; wi817 suite (15 tests incl sort_param_applier_witness) + wi418/wi419/wi613 + full workspace green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-23T16:52:39Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-825", author: "user", content: "NUMBER RECYCLED — disambiguation for readers: an earlier, UNRELATED WI-825 (scoped/named instance selection) was filed and then folded into WI-648 earlier the same day (see WI-648's feedback 'FOLD-IN from WI-825 ... now deleted in its favor' and commit 4cf167c8's subject); the CLI reissued the freed number to THIS ticket. Any WI-825 reference recorded before 2026-07-23T13:00Z means the folded instance-selection ticket (now WI-648); this ticket is the compound-element σ-gate fix from the WI-821 /code-review.", at: "2026-07-23T13:34:41Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-825", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED as specified — the ticket's prediction was exact: driven pre-fix measurements matched verbatim (single hand-off 12, recursion 12 at EVERY depth, positive control 122), and the fix locus was ONE place. sigma_pair_precise's (c,c) arm now compares a both-compound pair sigma-STRUCTURALLY: same base sort (same_sort_canonical) + per-argument recursion (sigma-classes at param leaves, dispatch_values_match at ground leaves); named args paired via the shared binding-key rule (binding_for_param + BindingKeyMatch::for_bases — enrolled per /simplify review, NOT a fifth hand-rolled find(same_label)); a==b fast path restores O(1) for identical hash-consed compounds (identical term = identical instantiation). The shared verdict had THREE consumers, not two: binding_pair_covers (entries_cover + requires_entry_covers_goal), entry_sigma_matches_subst (WI-613 tie-break), reached_carrier_matches_call (WI-653 transitive coverage) — all compound-aware now, header names all three. Coarse (None) mode untouched per WATCH; ground same-head pairs still cover (wi825 ground_compound_cover_still_serves). ACCEPTANCE MET: wi825_compound_element_test measures 122 + 12/122/1222 (4 tests, incl the no-cover positive control); wi817 15/15 incl sort_param_applier_witness; wi828 + wi418/wi419/wi613 green; full workspace 85/85 result lines 0 failed (x2 runs, jobs capped 6). NAMED RESIDUAL (no ticket): both-ARROW/both-NAMED-TUPLE element pairs still accept via dispatch_values_match's head fallback (same meta-ctor symbol, interiors ignored) — same defect class, unclosed because no sigma-gated path is known to carry those forms as elements; documented at parameterized_parts.", at: "2026-07-23T16:52:39Z")
